      <p class="text-[11px] italic">
        Listed alphabetically (19 total). Each carries `isEstimated: true` with an explicit `estimationDisclaimer` describing its triangulation source.
      </p>
      <p>
        For these economies, data is derived using a multi-source triangulation framework:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 my-2 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-border/60 bg-background/50">
          <strong class="text-foreground block mb-1">1. UN Humanitarian Monitoring</strong>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground">Market price surveillance and vulnerability assessments by the UN World Food Programme (WFP VAM) and UN FAO GIEWS.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-border/60 bg-background/50">
          <strong class="text-foreground block mb-1">2. Regional PPP Parity Models</strong>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground">World Bank International Comparison Program (ICP) purchasing power parity regression benchmarks and neighboring country baskets.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-lg border border-border/60 bg-background/50">
          <strong class="text-foreground block mb-1">3. Cross-Border & Informal Data</strong>
          <span class="text-muted-foreground">For closed economies like North Korea, informal market surveys (Jangmadang market basket reports from Daily NK / Asia Press) and Bank of Korea models.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        All estimated economies are explicitly labeled with an <span class="text-amber-500 font-semibold">"Est." badge</span> and detailed disclaimers across all tables, charts, and comparison tools.
      </p>
